values ('bbbb0005-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e', 'en', null, 'Medieval Europe: The Middle Ages', 'The thousand years between the fall of Rome and the dawn of the Renaissance, from roughly 500 to 1500 CE — kingdoms and crusades, cathedrals and plague, faith and famine. The topic framing and dates are drawn from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0), but every word of the prose here is original. By the end you will be able to explain how Europe reshaped itself after Rome and why the medieval world matters.', null, 'foundations', 54, true, 'humanities', '{}')
